Then my mother passed away that junkie'd had a long stay\
You weren't at the funeral not many remember you\
The ones who do look away ashamed of their memories\
\
But I remember find you\
In the lowest of going down town\
No more falling this is as far south as it is before hell\
\
I woke you with a kiss in moments of death\
You wake hours later ashamed of life and\
Say dreams are something you wake up from\
Nightmares chase you through the day\
You say your dreams were stolen from you\
They cant take your dreams away\
You gave it away each day\
Only you can give away\
\
Fields down below\
Where the rivers run down to the sea\
Too hot sun is cooled in Lorien streams\
Emerald grass golden sands\
We built the house of our dreams\
It stands there for you\
